If a patient has an opioid-use-disorder during a pregnancy then every clinician should offer an opioid-use-disorder-medication to the patient at an earliest-possible-pregnancy-time during a patient-and-fetus-harm-prevention.
If a patient has an opioid-use-disorder during a pregnancy then every clinician may offer a buprenorphine to the patient.
If a patient has an opioid-use-disorder during a pregnancy then every clinician may offer a methadone to the patient.
